00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:04.900
Speaker 1: I have a great example for you
today of techniques to counter propaganda.

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:12.630
Many times people will ask How is it best
to react when someone asserts this or says

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:13.630
that?

00:00:13.630 --> 00:00:17.830
And you know that their reason for bringing
it up is a bad faith reason or the premise

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:19.419
is wrong or whatever the case may be.

00:00:19.419 --> 00:00:24.769
So we're going to talk about this today using
an example from Fox News reporter Peter Doocy,

00:00:24.769 --> 00:00:30.519
who's always trying to make himself look as
big and strong and like a real reporter and

00:00:30.519 --> 00:00:33.430
like a guy who asks important questions.

00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:40.880
And the technique here is ask for examples
when you are given a premise and you know

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:45.800
that the premise is shaky or it's being used
to make a point that doesn't actually follow.

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:48.830
The first thing is make them defend the premise.

00:00:48.830 --> 00:00:50.480
Don't just accept it.

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:56.360
And Fox's Peter Doocy asked White House Press
Secretary Jen Psaki about the don't say gay

00:00:56.360 --> 00:01:05.670
bill from Florida, and the question he asked
was Does the White House support teaching

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:11.079
kids younger than kindergarten, sex education
or gender educate, you know, whatever the

00:01:11.079 --> 00:01:12.609
case may be.

00:01:12.609 --> 00:01:19.290
And Jen Psaki smartly says, Do you even have
examples of when that's being done?

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:24.280
Because if you don't, you're really just saying,
will Biden denounce something that's not even

00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:25.280
going on?

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:28.069
And that's what we would define as a pointless
question to answer.

00:01:28.069 --> 00:01:30.350
So let's look at the clip and then we're going
to talk about it.

00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:36.759
Speaker 3: So if you guys oppose this law
that bans classroom instruction about sexual

00:01:36.759 --> 00:01:41.219
orientation and gender identity in K through
three, does the White House support that kind

00:01:41.219 --> 00:01:43.090
of classroom instruction before kindergarten?

00:01:43.090 --> 00:01:47.899
Speaker 4: Do you have examples of schools
in Florida that are teaching kindergartners

00:01:47.899 --> 00:01:50.310
about sex education, asking for the president?

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:54.779
I think that's a I think that's a relevant
question because I think this is a politically

00:01:54.779 --> 00:02:04.450
charged harsh law that is putting parents
and LGBTQ plus kids in a very difficult, a

00:02:04.450 --> 00:02:06.470
heartbreaking circumstance.

00:02:06.470 --> 00:02:08.600
And so I actually think that's a pretty relevant
question.

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:12.440
Speaker 1: So this is a really good technique,
and I'm going to talk about it a little more

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:13.710
in a second.

00:02:13.710 --> 00:02:18.700
So first of all, understand that what Steve
Doocy, Peter Doocy brings up.

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:19.860
It's it's just not happening.

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:22.030
It's not happening.

00:02:22.030 --> 00:02:29.310
First of all, when we talk about sexual orientation
instruction, the don't say gay bill is about

00:02:29.310 --> 00:02:35.270
in K through three, and Doocy goes further
